---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'How It Works',href:'/how-it-works/'}];
const stages=[
 ['Define the Trip','Who is traveling, why they are going, dates, source markets, activity, comfort, budget, and constraints.','◎'],
 ['Shape the Plan','Compare realistic destinations and build route, lodging, transport, activities, operators, and support.','⌖'],
 ['Prepare to Launch','Organize the information participants need to understand the trip and decide whether it fits.','▤'],
 ['Confirm the Group','Bring traveler commitments, supplier terms, deposits, rooming, and key assumptions into a confirmed picture.','✓'],
 ['Prepare to Travel','Resolve documents, equipment, readiness, arrivals, provider requirements, and final travel information.','▣'],
 ['Travel Supported','Make the support structure clear and define who is responsible for each important part of the trip.','↗']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="How Group Travel Planning Works | Talon Expeditions" description="How Talon Expeditions moves a group trip from early idea through itinerary design, participant launch, confirmation, traveler preparation, and supported departure." image={images.planning} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="av-inner-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="shell"><h1>How It Works</h1><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="av-services-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The Operating Model</p><h2>A Group Trip Is a Sequence of Decisions, Not a Shopping Cart</h2><p>Talon Expeditions uses a staged planning process that starts with the group and progressively reduces uncertainty. The goal is to answer the questions that affect the next commitment before the organizer or travelers are asked to make it.</p></div><div class="av-service-grid">{stages.map((stage,index)=><div class="av-service-card"><div class="av-service-card-icon">{stage[2]}</div><span class="av-blog-meta">Stage 0{index+1}</span><h3>{stage[0]}</h3><p>{stage[1]}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="av-proof-band" style={`background-image:url('${images.train}')`}><div class="shell"><div class="av-proof-head"><p class="eyebrow">What Changes as the Trip Develops</p><h2>Early flexibility becomes later certainty.</h2></div><div class="av-proof-grid"><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>Early Planning</h3><p>Broad ranges are useful: destination options, likely dates, group size, budget, activity level, and support model.</p><small>Explore</small></div><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>Proposal Stage</h3><p>Route, lodging, suppliers, inclusions, payment structure, minimum group assumptions, and terms become more specific.</p><small>Commit</small></div><div class="av-proof-card"><h3>Confirmed Trip</h3><p>Traveler details, rooming, documents, equipment, flights, final schedules, support contacts, and supplier confirmations become the operating authority.</p><small>Prepare</small></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="av-process"><div class="shell av-process-grid"><div class="av-process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}><div class="av-process-callout"><h3>The Process Should Get Quieter</h3><p>As departure approaches, the core plan should become more settled, explicit, and easier to follow.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Organizer Communication</p><h2>Participants Should Not Need to Reverse-Engineer the Trip From Email Threads</h2><p class="av-process-lead">As the plan becomes real, traveler information should become more consolidated. The organizer needs a clear way to explain what is decided, what is still open, what participants need to do, and when decisions are required.</p><div class="av-process-topline"><strong>Start before every detail is solved</strong><a href="/plan-a-trip/">↗</a></div><div class="av-process-steps"><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▤</div><div><h3>Trip Overview</h3><p>Dates, purpose, itinerary concept, who it suits, and important assumptions.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">$</div><div><h3>Inclusions & Milestones</h3><p>What is included, what is not, and when decisions or payments are due.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">✓</div><div><h3>Readiness</h3><p>Activity expectations, equipment, documents, rooming, and participant requirements.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">⌖</div><div><h3>Final Travel Picture</h3><p>Arrival details, confirmed itinerary, local roles, and support contacts.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
